<!--
  BlockML Core — bootstrap documentation

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.documentation.DocumentationModel
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition"
  xmlns:lang="org.blockml.bml.language"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <idea>Block documentation model — idea, documentation, references, examples, README, documentation blocks.</idea>

  <documentation>
    Every root block definition carries a documentation model at the definition site — single
    source of truth inside BML files:

    idea (required, first child) — semantic meaning of the Block; the stable constant (WOT: Idea).
    language (optional) — natural language for documentation prose; inherits Library → Block
      default (English on org.blockml.bml.core.Block).
    documentation (required, second child) — technical description of the Block definition itself;
      optional language attribute when prose deviates from effective block language.
    Member elements carry their own documentation for individual Properties, Aggregations, etc.

    Optional extensions (wherever documentation is permitted):
    since — version from which the element is available
    changelog — container of change entries (oldest first)
    examples — container of example entries (title in block natural language + CDATA body)
    references — container of see entries (block, file, or url + relationship text)

    Natural language inheritance (documentation prose and example titles):
    Library.language → Block.language → documentation / change / see language attribute
    Unqualified names inside &lt;language&gt; and on documentation, change, and see language=
    resolve via org.blockml.bml.language.*. Authors declare language only when deviating from
    the effective inherited language. Example title language always follows the enclosing block — example
    language attribute applies to CDATA content only (implementation dialect: OpenSCAD,
    TypeScript, …) and also resolves via org.blockml.bml.language.*.

    Authoring split:
    • documentation carries technical prose only
    • references carries all cross-links — Blocks, Definition elements, repository markdown
      files, and external URLs — each with an explicit relationship note
    • Do not repeat cross-links in documentation prose

    see target attributes (exactly one required):
    block="core:ValueType" — Block or Definition via xmlns prefix
    file="02_mbml.md" — repository documentation file
    url="https://…" — external URL

    README blocks (baseType org.blockml.bml.core.Bootstrap) expose readFirst — an ordered list of
    Documentation block instances for mental bootstrap reading order. Documentation blocks
    (org.blockml.bml.documentation.*) inherit from org.blockml.bml.core.Documentation.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see file="02_mbml.md">
      idea, documentation, since, changelog, examples, references — authoring rules.
    </see>
    <see file="16_framework_base_types.md">
      Definition branch documentation model — ReferenceDefinition meta-model.
    </see>
    <see file="12_bom_object_model.md">
      DocumentationExample, DocumentationReference — BOM documentation shapes.
    </see>
    <see file="01_system.md">
      V2 documentation migration — Markdown vs BML roles.
    </see>
    <see block="lang:NaturalLanguage">
      Natural language branch — documentation prose and example titles.
    </see>
    <see block="core:Block">
      Root block — documents idea, language, documentation, references on every definition.
    </see>
    <see block="core:Definition">
      Definition branch — shared documentation aggregations.
    </see>
    <see block="def:DocumentationDefinition">
      Meta-model for documentation elements on Definition branch types.
    </see>
    <see block="def:ReferenceDefinition">
      Meta-model for see entries inside references.
    </see>
    <see block="def:ExampleDefinition">
      Meta-model for example entries inside examples.
    </see>
    <see block="core:Documentation">
      Abstract base for narrative documentation blocks in readFirst lists.
    </see>
    <see block="core:Bootstrap">
      Bootstrap base — readFirst aggregation for README blocks.
    </see>
    <see block="doc:BootstrapModel">
      Next reading step — README.bml, readFirst, bootstrap context.
    </see>
  </references>

  <name>DocumentationModel</name>
  <type>doc:DocumentationModel</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>

</block>
